{"availability":"available","full":"stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo","name":"0sql-dashboard-demo","description":"Chat-driven analytics dashboard on the 0sql semantic layer API: Claude writes query specs, 0sql plans the SQL, your app runs it.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-05T20:56:17Z","updated":"2026-10-09T14:06:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["0sql","analytics","claude","duckdb","nextjs","semantic-layer"],"demo":"https://0sql.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.822Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.822Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.822Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.822Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A custom analytics dashboard where the questions are typed in English and the SQL is planned by 0sql. The model writes a query spec; 0sql turns that spec into one correct SQL statement for the warehouse, with row-level security compiled in; the app runs it and draws it. Say \"pin that\" and the answer becomes a dashboard tile. Claude drives it by default and OpenAI works too — the spec is the contract, not the provider.","The model never writes SQL and never sees a connection string. It cannot invent a join, pick the wrong grain, or step around a security policy, because none of those are its to decide — they live in a semantic model you deploy. When it does get a spec wrong, 0sql refuses with a class and a message, and the agent fixes it on the next turn.","Everything here is open: the dashboard app, the semantic model it queries, and the synthetic warehouse the SQL runs against."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5ce466ccf09b3b36dbdd907f56887f15061dbb9531c3c63ee62d0d3fa5290590","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.916Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.916Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A custom analytics dashboard where the questions are typed in English and the SQL is planned by 0sql. The model writes a query spec; 0sql turns that spec into one correct SQL statement for the warehouse, with row-level security compiled in; the app runs it and draws it. Say \"pin that\" and the answer becomes a dashboard tile. Claude drives it by default and OpenAI works too — the spec is the contract, not the provider.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Around that sit subject areas a question reaches only when it asks for them — memberships, A/B allocations, help center traffic — joined through the customer's account and subscription.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5ce466ccf09b3b36dbdd907f56887f15061dbb9531c3c63ee62d0d3fa5290590","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.916Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T14:06:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stratasite/0sql-dashboard-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.917Z","hash":"5ce466ccf09b3b36dbdd907f56887f15061dbb9531c3c63ee62d0d3fa5290590","originalBytes":17949,"storedBytes":17949,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["model","sql","contact","one","query","what","src","spec","which","prompt","run","warehouse","app","cost","lib","semantic","dashboard","does","key","call","every","fields","own","center","how","same","agent","deploy","only","region","them","they","tile","two","where","api","customer","npm","openai","passed","per","planned","rate","table","tables","answer","each","field","last","plan","policy","question","security","supervisor","there","under","usd","against","amer","anthropic","context","driver","fact",